// A stamp mill with no room at its foot holds its work. Rock stands against its right side and its drive gear
// against its left, so it has nowhere to let crushed ore out: the ore waits in its mortar unbroken and the log says
// its spout is walled in (before, what it crushed went back into it and was lost, a lump at a time).
map
##################################
##################################
#....jj*jjjjjjj*.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j.................#
#..............j....#............#
#..........@...*....#............#
##################################
##################################
end
give Counterweight 2
give StampMill 1
place 2 -7 -8 Counterweight
place 2 -4 -7 Counterweight
place 3 7 -1 StampMill
drop 10 CopperOre 6 -7
drop 20 CopperOre 6 -7
expect 600 log:spout_is_walled_in >= 1
expect 1800 stampload == 2            // both lumps still there, whole
expect 1800 items:CopperFines == 0
expect 1800 items:Sand == 0
